/* ===== cameo characters ported from the 1.x fork =====
 *
 * PLACEHOLDER PARTIES. None of these characters is a trainer in the fork - only
 * their sprites exist there - so there is nothing to port for their teams and
 * the single mon below is a stub. Replace before placing any of them.
 *
 * They share TRAINER_CLASS_PKMN_TRAINER_1_HNS, the tree's existing cameo class
 * (Red and Steven already use it), so the intro reads "{PKMN} TRAINER CYNTHIA".
 * A class per character would render as "CYNTHIA CYNTHIA".
 *
 * NOTE: that class currently has no money multiplier, so these battles pay 0.
 *
 * Alder and Bato reuse `Pic: Red Hns` as an explicit placeholder - their fork
 * sprites were deliberately not ported.
 *
 * GENDER IS NOT COSMETIC. CreateNPCTrainerPartyFromTrainer picks the party's
 * personality seed from it (battle_main.c: TRAINER_GENDER_FEMALE -> 0x78, else
 * 0x88), which biases the gender of every Pokemon the trainer fields. These
 * headers were written from one template and all said Male; Cynthia, Iris and
 * both Soras are female and now say so, before the real parties land and
 * inherit the wrong bias. Buck, Alder, Yama and Bato are male - Bato confirmed
 * by Moritz, 2026-08-29, since there is no art or source to check it against.
 */

